p = "experiments/E344_e2e-completion-plan/experiment.md"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()


def rep(a, b, cnt=1):
    global s
    assert s.count(a) == cnt, (s.count(a), a[:80])
    s = s.replace(a, b)


def between(start, end, new):
    global s
    i = s.index(start)
    j = s.index(end)
    s = s[:i] + new + s[j:]


between("## 4. Track B: Q-Lane, one query head on the 1 m grid", "### 4b. Variant B0", """## 4. Track B: Q-Lane, one query head on the 1 m grid
**Idea (what we talked about before: E294 "nodes from the 1 m maps", E295 "a position spread per node", E297 "soft pruning", D82 "stay differentiable"):** every cell of the 1 m grid (100 x 100 = 10 000, on the same frozen pyramid as today, so comparisons stay fair) is a query. No Hungarian matching: the queries are anchored at their cell like the 2 m nodes of B and like the end heat of E307 (CenterNet style), which keeps the training easy on 8 414 frames; free DETR-style queries (TP30, TP05, TP06 in the corpus) are kept as the later option B2 (the claim that they converge slowly on 8 414 frames is from the literature, not measured here). **Read section 1b first:** the pyramid already has a dense 1 m `centre1` head whose node F1 (0.612) was far below B's 2 m heads (0.772 / 0.776, E273); that is the reason B has 2 m cells, and Q-Lane has to say what is different.
**What a query outputs:** an existence logit; a type (normal, split, merge, entry, exit, as B has them); a sub-cell position mean and a position uncertainty (sigma along and across the line: the Laplace NLL of E318, the heat target of sigma 1.0 m of E307); a heading with a concentration; and a successor distribution over a fixed set of forward slots in the query's own frame plus a dustbin ("no successor here"), computed densely by a convolutional head. Open points that Q0 decides, because they are not details: (a) **one query per cell, one heading, one successor distribution cannot hold crossing connectors** (1.9 % of the lane cells at 1 m, 3.5 % of the connector cells hold connectors more than 45 degrees apart; section 1b); (b) **connector length against the slot radius:** 73.5 % of the GT connectors are longer than a 12 m slot radius, the median is 19 m; (c) **how a slot becomes an edge:** the softmax is normalised over positions, not nodes; B's soft walk (`sections.py:17-33`, a backward walk over the incoming-link logits of candidate pairs plus a "no predecessor" option, a dense K x K `linalg.solve` with K = 512, 2.80 ms) needs node-to-node edges, so a slot needs a nearest-node choice or a soft attach (the selection problem of E320 / E325 again), and a dense walk over 10 000 queries is impossible (a 10^4 x 10^4 solve; at 1 m density K rises to about 500 - 650 and the cost scales as K^3): **an active set (a top-K and a threshold) is unavoidable and stays a named rule step**; (d) what happens to B's assigner (`qassign.py`, 8.33 ms, the biggest B head, reads B's node tokens).
**Junction connectors: two representations, both tested by Q0, decided by its numbers:** (i) chains of ordinary nodes through the junction (every 1 - 2 m; about 300 extra nodes per junction frame at 1 m, 150 at 2 m, against 159 nodes per frame for all lanes in B; crossing connectors share cells), or (ii) the connector stays a Hermite link between two sharp ends (as B's long links and as E312 / E324 s do) and only its interior carries a large sigma (section 4b); (i) and (ii) contradict each other in the first version of this plan; B's own rule since E273 is (ii) ("connectors carry no nodes").
**Output:** a probabilistic graph: nodes with existence, type, mean, sigma, heading; edges with probabilities. The planner (and the time fusion of D90 / D91) reads probabilities and uncertainties; what is left is the consumer's thresholds T and the active set of the walk.
**One loss for everything** (the "optimises smoothness and connections and everything" part). What exists and what does not: existence: BCE with pos_weight 20 + dice (E307, `jmaps_loss`; focal lives in `qendnet.py` / `qgraph.py`); type CE; position: the Laplace NLL exists for ends only (`jends.py`, E318 running); heading cosine; successor CE with the dustbin (new); **duplicate suppression as a one-to-one loss: only E292's damping layer `qmnms.py` exists, and it is a hypothesis against two negative results (section 1b): the card of Q1c must say how a one-to-one matching differs from that damping when the GT neighbours are 1 m apart**; **smoothness (curvature of the soft path, C1 continuity of the tangent): no code exists**; connector geometry (the Chamfer loss of E317, running); the order / non-crossing penalty (E287); a keep-gate budget (`qkeep.py` is "to write" in E297; only E271's `soft_lines.sparsify` exists).
**Stages and gates** (every stage a card with its rule before the run, a predicted number, two seeds, VAL, a paired scene bootstrap, an equal-step control (the pair-stage noise has never been measured, E318 revision item 1), a fresh critic; one refinement round on a TIE; **GPU stages wait for a recorded decision D<n> of Mirko on D84 point 6 and on B's heads; Q0 may run under D86**):
| stage | what | cost | gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| Q0 (card E347) | representation ceiling, CPU, GT only, 1 m and 2 m: render the GT graph into the query code (existence, type, offset, heading, successor slots, both connector representations), decode with the soft read-out, score with `qgraph_eval.score_frames` on VAL 873 | days of code, no GPU | topo F1 of the decoded GT at least B's own representation oracle (`qformat.oracle_prediction`, same frames, same scorer; E273 l.284: 0.97) minus 0.005, degraded null copies (shifted, thinned, headings flipped as `test_oracle.py`) that must fall, and a reproduction control (2 m, connectors suppressed: E273's decode coverage, lane 99.98 %, connectors 93.4 %); nodes per 100 m, K and the walk's K per grid reported |
| Q1a | dense 1 m node head with a sub-cell offset on the frozen pyramid (E294 revived; node scorer adapted to 1 m nodes against 2 m GT: the scorer contract has `cell` on a 2 m grid, `qformat.py:7`) | 4 - 6 GPU h per seed | node F1 within 0.01 of B's 0.8525 / 0.8505, vertices at most the control + 1.0, convolution-only head (ms of B's node head 2.88 + 1 ms; local attention grows with the cells: four times the cells is about four times 2.9 ms) |
| Q1b | + sigma (after E318 has run) | 2 - 4 GPU h per seed | ENCE reported, node F1 within 0.01 of Q1a |
| Q1c | + soft keep gate (E297) and the one-to-one loss | 4 - 6 GPU h per seed | duplicates and vertices against Q1a, the one-to-one loss against E292 arm a's damping |
| Q2 | + successor links and the soft sections, replacing B's links / sections (5.46 + 2.80 ms); the assigner decided | 6 - 8 GPU h per seed | B's plain delivered graph (VAL: topo F1 0.6259 / 0.6249, B plus the hard close-node step on 873 frames): within 0.01, lanes found within 0.015, the assignment guard of E292 (lane_acc 0.9805 / 0.9498) held |
| Q3 | + junction: dense entry / exit types, connector chains or links; no snap, no top-K peak choice, no close-node step | 8 - 12 GPU h per seed | ONE pairing: the unsnapped read-out within 0.01 of E324 s unsnapped, whose stored card does not exist (`runs/e324_s_s*/ends_card_thr0.1.json` is missing: scored on the CPU first; E312 unsnapped 0.6438 / 0.6481, E324 s PRIMARY 0.6912 / 0.6948, snapped 0.6981 / 0.7010); a cheap early probe of the connector part before Q2 is part of the Q3 card |
| Q4 | joint training of everything with the smoothness and geometry losses; calibration of the existence and of sigma | 8 - 12 GPU h per seed | equal-accuracy bar + ECE / ENCE reported; smoothness measured (curvature of the delivered lines against the GT's) |
| Q5 | the system against E324 s on VAL, two seeds, then ONE TEST with Mirko's own recorded OK | CPU + short GPU | at most two R steps; accuracy within the bar |
Total GPU: 52 - 76 slot hours for two seeds from the per-stage costs above (the first version said 60 - 100). There is no step-time basis for them: the training step of the pair stage is host-bound at about 1.0 - 1.4 s (E330 section 2), the dense target render is unmeasured, and jobs of 8 - 12 hours do not fit the nights and the Mon - Fri 08:30 - 15:30 window that D100 kept (a weekend, or a resume across windows). The plan is cut after any stage that fails its gate twice, and the report says which rule steps remain. **E345 / E346 (D99) size the heads that Q-Lane would replace**: their Pareto table sets Q-Lane's width and ms budget (D92: width 64), so E345 runs first.
**Alternatives considered:** (B1) keep the junction layer and replace only the top-K by a soft token set (all cells weighted by their heat, attention instead of a hard index choice): small, but it keeps the snap, the wiring and the close-node step; (B2) free DETR-style queries with Hungarian matching inside the loss: allowed by D55, the literature has it (TP30 and followers), parked by D84 point 6; (B3) do nothing beyond track A: the R steps stay named, each with its measured price.

""")

